<details id="browser-recovery-panel" class="browser-recovery-panel">
<summary id="browser-recovery-summary">Keep work on this browser, optional</summary>
<p id="browser-recovery-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Saving is off. Keep a downloaded backup before leaving.</p>
<p class="small" id="browser-recovery-help">One recovery copy can stay on this browser after closing or refreshing. It includes your article, source notes, and saved review questions, in unencrypted site storage. Anyone using this browser profile may restore it. It does not sync to another device or save pending imports, unsaved editing tools, collections, or revision history. Only one tab can save at a time. Saving must be enabled again after reopening.</p>
<label class="check"><input id="browser-recovery-consent" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="browser-recovery-help"><span>I allow an unencrypted copy of this workspace, including private notes, to be kept on this browser.</span></label>
<div class="actions"><button id="browser-recovery-start" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Enable browser recovery</button><button id="browser-recovery-restore" type="button" class="secondary" disabled hidden>Restore copy and resume saving</button><button id="browser-recovery-now" type="button" class="secondary" hidden>Save recovery now</button><button id="browser-recovery-pause" type="button" class="secondary" hidden>Pause saving, keep copy</button><button id="browser-recovery-forget" type="button" class="secondary" hidden>Remove browser copy</button></div>
<p id="browser-recovery-date" class="small"></p><p class="small">Browser storage can be unavailable or cleared. For important writing, also use <a href="#workspace-tools">a downloaded private backup</a>. Nothing is uploaded or published.</p>
</details>
